# Cloudflare Pages response headers for the standalone Expo web export
# (app.boardsesh.com). See ./README.md for the full rationale, especially the
# hard CSP constraint.
#
# HARD RULE: never add a Content-Security-Policy with a `script-src` here. The
# board-renderer WASM glue instantiates its module via `new Function(...)`, so it
# needs `unsafe-eval` / `wasm-unsafe-eval`. A strict script-src breaks the
# renderer.

/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Content-hashed assets (filenames change when content changes) — cache forever.
/_expo/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# index.html and wasm/* keep fixed filenames, so they deliberately get NO cache
# override here — they must revalidate, or a deploy would be masked by a stale
# cached shell / stale WASM binary. (Left to Pages' default caching.)
